  "tagline": "Decentralised, offline-first graph database that syncs peer-to-peer in JavaScript.",
  "description": "GUN is a small JavaScript graph database where every browser or Node process is a peer: data is a graph of nodes merged with a CRDT-like conflict algorithm (HAM), replicated over WebSockets, WebRTC or relay peers, and persisted locally (RAD storage on disk or IndexedDB). The SEA module adds user accounts, signing and encryption in user space. It is popular for hobby decentralised apps, chat and experiments because it needs no central server. It has no transactions, a quirky API, thin documentation, and eventual consistency that makes it unsuitable for data needing invariants.",
